MID_SE_Oly_Ale_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_C_001: *sigh*
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_C_002: Is something the matter? That was quite a moody\nsigh that escaped from you just now.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_C_003: Oh, Olympia. It's...nothing. Some soldiers who look\ndown on my house were just being cruel.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_C_004: Bad-mouthing me and saying I've lived a sheltered\nlife, that I've never known any hardship.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_C_005: Pay them no heed, Alexandra. Malicious talk like\nthat should not be taken to heart.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_C_006: Let them say what they like, but do not let it\nget the better of you.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_C_007: Thanks. That's good advice.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_C_008: But my uncle did make me wield the Arc to give me\nan unfair advantage in the Heroic Games.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_C_009: And he used his powerful influence with the temples\nto do all kinds of dishonest things.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_C_010: Of course, you don't get to choose your family. No\namount of talking it out is going to change anything.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_C_011: Hmm...
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_C_012: I used to vent about it to Bucephalus, but even he\ncan only take so much of my wallowing.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_C_013: So you've been suffering on your own, have you?\nWell, you don't need to do that any longer.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_C_014: Listen. When I first arrived at Kalla's temple, not\na day went by without someone speaking ill of me.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_C_015: They mocked me for daring to challenge Leilidahna.\nThey said I didn't know my place.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_C_016: It was awful, and I hated it. But I didn't let it get to\nme. One must steel one's heart against such things!
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_C_017: I'm not as tough as you though.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_C_018: Then you need to get tougher. It's as simple as that.\nBut do not worry—I shall guide you.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_C_019: First, imagine that I'm the little coward who bad-\nmouthed you. Next...give me a piece of your mind!
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_C_020: Huh? I don't think I could ever say something\nmean to you.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_C_021: Go on now. I am a cruel and slanderous villain!\nSpeak your mind!
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_C_022: Um, well... I hate you! I hate you? But maybe I don't.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_C_023: No, no. That's not it. Ugh. I'm not good at this.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_C_024: My word!
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_C_025: I'm sorry. I know you're trying to help me here.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_C_026: Raise your head and look at me. I'm actually\nvery impressed!
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_C_027: You didn't use foul language, and you refused to say\na lie. You are sweet and true, and THAT is a virtue.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_C_028: Thank you, Olympia.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_C_029: I think that you should put that innocent heart of\nyours to good use and compose a poem.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_C_030: A poem? But I'm a knight. We're not really known\nfor our artistic pursuits.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_C_031: OK, I'll do it. You're offering to help me, and nothing\nis going to change if I don't try something.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_B_001: Olympia!
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_B_002: I did what you suggested before! I wrote a poem, and\nI'd love for you to hear it!
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_B_003: Wonderful! I can't wait. What is it about?
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_B_004: It's a little embarrassing, but I wrote it about\nsomething I find beautiful.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_B_005: Oh my, I like that! But I'm curious to hear what\npretty thing inspired you to pen this poem.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_B_006: Now, just remember this is my first poem.\nIt's probably not good, so try and be gentle...
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_B_007: Do not fret. I'm sure I'll enjoy hearing whatever\nyou've written.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_B_008: OK, OK. Here goes.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_B_009: "Olympia, you're so fair, and noble, and true,\nThere's no one I've met as perfunctory as you."
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_B_010: Oh...oh my...
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_B_011: I hope you don't mind. The poem's about you! I was\ninspired by your beauty.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_B_012: Is that so?!
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_B_013: Never mind. A poem by a novice like me is going\nto be terrible anyway.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_B_014: No, no, not at all! It's just that I was surprised to\nhear that you admire my beauty.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_B_015: Come now, pay me no mind. Carry on with\nyour poem.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_B_016: Ahem. "Your face is so interestingly shaped,\nLike a pear or maybe a grape."
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_B_017: I've never heard a poem quite like that before. You\nhave so much to say... A loquacious talent indeed.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_B_018: That's a real honor coming from you, Olympia, the\nBlue Rose of Caelus.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_B_019: Thank you. But I do have one piece of advice.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_B_020: How do I put this? Your subject matter needs more\nvariety...and your stanzas need fewer words.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_B_021: You noticed that too? I knew there was something...\nThere's a lot of room for improvement here.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_B_022: Ah, you were already aware of that? What a relief.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_B_023: Maybe next time, instead of writing a poem about\nyour beauty, I'll write about your strength!
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_B_024: Y-you're going to write another whole poem\nabout...me?!
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_B_025: Of course! Whenever I think of you and work on a\npoem, all those cruel voices I've heard just disappear.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_B_026: {SetColor=Gray}I did suggest she try to take her mind off the\npeople whispering behind her back.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_B_027: {SetColor=Gray}I just didn't imagine THIS is how she'd do it.\nHer poems are so very...terrible.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_B_028: Is something wrong?
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_B_029: No, I'm just pleased to see you enjoying your new\npastime. And I want to hear more of your writing!
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_B_030: But if you don't mind, why don't we keep these\npoems of yours just between us?
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_B_031: *gasp* You'd like it to be something special\nthat only we share? That sounds lovely.
MID_SE_Oly_Ale_B_032: Yes, yes. That is exactly what I meant. Oh goodness,\nthis really has cheered you up, hasn't it?